  m_Name: MechanicalMemory
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GravityBox.Gameplay::GravityBox.Gameplay.LevelDefinition
  Id: steel-lab-mechanicalmemory
  DisplayIndex: 22
  DisplayName: The box remembers
  Shape: 21
  TeachingHint: Push the rack, return, push again. The ratchet remembers each physical
    stroke.
  Environment: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 82e0ce24addfe4fc89b8bbd0db998aea, type: 2}
  Prefab: {fileID: 2767367283102442559, guid: 8339d7594af944ed4b633ddce785c462, type: 3}
  RotationMode: 1
  InitialLocalVelocity: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  ParSeconds: 0
  Tutorial: 0
  DesignerSolution: The ball physically compresses a spring-return rack, transferring
    contact force into a rotating cam. A retaining pawl constraint prevents backward
    motion after each reached tooth; a bounded rack stroke prevents skipping several
    stages. Read the physical cam and path position, repeat strokes, then cross the
    opened route. No timer or invisible trigger rotates the cam. Shared exit assist
    pulls the ball through an unobstructed opening within 40 mm. This is deliberate
    gameplay assistance; the entire sphere must still physically clear the bore before
    completion.
